===Etymology===
Cognate with {{cog|br|blev}} and {{cog|cy|blew}}. Of uncertain ultimate origin and lacking Celtic cognates outside of Brythonic. Perhaps related to {{cog|grc|φλόος|t=rind, bark}}.<ref>Language. (1931). United States: Linguistic Society of America, p. 239</ref> Or, related to {{cog|lt|plùskos|t=hair}} and {{cog|gmw-pro|*fleus|t=fleece}}, from {{der|kw|ine-pro|*plews-|t=to pull out, pluck}}.<ref>{{R:ine:IEW|838}}</ref>

